  "body": "## Finding description and impact\nin `VotingEscrow`, any token with pending rewards merged as `from` or splitted will lose all of its earned rewards\n\nthis happens due to the fact that when we merge a `from` Id or we split a main NFT Id we  `_burn` that NFT, and hence its owner will be `address(0)` and hence claims will be lost since amounts will be transferred to `address(0)`\n```solidity\nFile: VotingEscrow.sol\n1074:         locked[_from] = IVotingEscrow.LockedBalance(0, 0, false);\n1075:         _checkpoint(_from, _locked0, IVotingEscrow.LockedBalance(0, 0, false));\n1076:         _burn(_from);\n```\nthis is not an out-of-scope bug since it doesn't originate from the `RewardsDistributor` but it comes from not calling claim upon any merge/splitting.\n\nAlso this wouldn't be a user mistake since he assumes that those cases will be handled as developer said in his ` ve(3,3) Epoch Cycle, Rotation, and Reward Distribution / Rebase` are of concerns\n\nbut in addition to users losing their rewards, `gHybr` contract is also affected.\n\nsince `gHybr` contract settles withdrawals through splitting, this would happen.\n1. Users deposits 100e18 to `governanceHybr`\n2. `governanceHybr` earns `Hybr` rewards\n3. one user is willing withdraw, `claimRewards()` hasn't been called by the operator yet\n4. the user withdraw and the old ve Id owned by `governanceHybr` gets splitted and loses all old `hybr` rewards\n\nThe above scenario is more reaslistic since it doesn't involve a naive user mistake of not claiming before splitting\n### Impact\nLoss of user rewards upon merging/splitting\n\nLoss of rebase amounts given to `gHybr`\n## Recommended mitigation steps\ncall claim on the to be splitted Id and merged from Id",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n    function test_rewardsDistributor_lossOnSplitMerge() external {\n\n        // Enable splitting for this test contract\n        votingEscrow.toggleSplit(address(this), true);\n\n        skip(2 weeks);\n        // Create a veNFT lock\n        uint256 lockAmount = 1000 ether;\n        hybr.approve(address(votingEscrow), lockAmount);\n        uint256 tokenId = votingEscrow.create_lock(lockAmount, 86400 * 365 * 2);\n\n        // Fund RewardsDistributor with some rewards\n        // First, let the minter distribute some rewards\n        minter.update_period();\n\n        // Then manually add more rewards to ensure we have significant claimable amounts\n        uint256 rewardAmount = 100 ether;\n        hybr.transfer(address(rewardsDistributor), rewardAmount);\n\n        // Call checkpoint_token through the minter (which is the depositor)\n        vm.prank(address(minter));\n        rewardsDistributor.checkpoint_token();\n\n        // Advance time to accumulate some claimable rewards\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 1 weeks);\n\n        // Check claimable rewards before split\n        uint256 claimableBeforeSplit = rewardsDistributor.claimable(tokenId);\n        console.log(\"Claimable before split:\", claimableBeforeSplit);\n        console.log(\n            \"Time cursor before split:\",\n            rewardsDistributor.time_cursor_of(tokenId)\n        );\n        console.log(\"Last token time:\", rewardsDistributor.last_token_time());\n        console.log(\"Current timestamp:\", block.timestamp);\n\n        // If no claimable rewards, let's advance more time and add more rewards\n        if (claimableBeforeSplit == 0) {\n            vm.warp(block.timestamp + 2 weeks);\n            minter.update_period();\n\n            // Add more rewards and checkpoint again\n            hybr.transfer(address(rewardsDistributor), 200 ether);\n            vm.prank(address(minter));\n            rewardsDistributor.checkpoint_token();\n\n            claimableBeforeSplit = rewardsDistributor.claimable(tokenId);\n            console.log(\n                \"Claimable after more time and rewards:\",\n                claimableBeforeSplit\n            );\n        }\n\n        assertGt(\n            claimableBeforeSplit,\n            0,\n            \"Should have claimable rewards before split\"\n        );\n\n        // Split the NFT into two parts\n        uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](2);\n        amounts[0] = 600; // 60% of the lock\n        amounts[1] = 400; // 40% of the lock\n\n        uint256[] memory newTokenIds = votingEscrow.multiSplit(\n            tokenId,\n            amounts\n        );\n        assertEq(newTokenIds.length, 2, \"Should create 2 new NFTs\");\n\n        uint256 tokenId1 = newTokenIds[0];\n        uint256 tokenId2 = newTokenIds[1];\n\n        // Check that the original tokenId no longer exists\n        assertEq(\n            votingEscrow.ownerOf(tokenId),\n            address(0),\n            \"Original NFT should be burned\"\n        );\n\n        // Check claimable rewards for new NFTs - they should be 0 because time_cursor_of is reset\n        uint256 claimableAfterSplit1 = rewardsDistributor.claimable(tokenId1);\n        uint256 claimableAfterSplit2 = rewardsDistributor.claimable(tokenId2);\n\n        assertEq(\n            claimableAfterSplit1,\n            0,\n            \"New NFT 1 should have 0 claimable rewards due to lost time_cursor_of\"\n        );\n        assertEq(\n            claimableAfterSplit2,\n            0,\n            \"New NFT 2 should have 0 claimable rewards due to lost time_cursor_of\"\n        );\n\n        // Demonstrate the economic impact: rewards are permanently lost\n        uint256 totalLostRewards = claimableBeforeSplit;\n        assertGt(totalLostRewards, 0, \"Significant rewards should be lost\");\n\n        //i showing rewards gets burned, run with -vvvv\n        rewardsDistributor.claim(tokenId);// 98076556845719136296 is the burned amount\n    }\n```",
